<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06JZ">Remark <span data-tag="06JZ">9.4.6.15</span>.</a> Let $\kappa \leq \lambda $ be regular cardinals. For any $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, postcomposition with the tautological map $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{Ind}_{\kappa }^{\lambda }(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$ induces a map of diagram $\infty $-categories $\operatorname{Fun}(K, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \rightarrow \operatorname{Fun}(K, \operatorname{Ind}_{\kappa }^{\lambda }(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) )$, which admits a $(\kappa ,\lambda )$-finitary extension </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \theta : \operatorname{Ind}_{\kappa }^{\lambda }( \operatorname{Fun}(K, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) ) \rightarrow \operatorname{Fun}(K, \operatorname{Ind}_{\kappa }^{\lambda }(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) ). \]
</div>
<p> Proposition <a data-tag="06JW" href="/tag/06JW">9.4.6.12</a> implies that if $K$ is $\kappa $-small, then $\theta $ is fully faithful. Corollary <a data-tag="06JY" href="/tag/06JY">9.4.6.14</a> asserts that $\theta $ is an equivalence if $K$ is $\kappa $-small and $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is $\kappa _0$-sequentially cocomplete for some $\kappa _0 &lt; \kappa $. </p>
</article>
